module.step:
Source { url: String, password: String, tls: bool, connections: usize } with a Debug that never prints the password: url is mysql://user@host:port; tls requires TLS (rustls, the server's certificate checked against webpki's roots); connections is how many connections the read may open at once, at least 1. ImportReport { version: String, flavor: String, objects: usize, rows: usize, statements: usize, read: Duration, stored: Duration }: statements counts every statement sent to the store, begin_operation's among them. EngineError: Source(String), Store(StoreError), Unsupported(String).
trait Engine: Send + Sync, with async-trait:
fn id(&self) -> &'static str (cortex.engines.id, "mysql");
fn namespace(&self) -> &'static str ("engine_mysql");
async fn import(&self, store: &Store, source: &Source, design: Uuid, turn: Uuid) -> Result<ImportReport, EngineError>: reads the server first, holding no transaction in the store, then writes every row in one operation of the given open turn, as the plugin's own account (Account::Plugin(namespace)), through Store::write and begin_operation;
async fn write(&self, store: &Store, design: Uuid) -> Result<String, EngineError>: loads the design's rows as the plugin's account through Store::read and returns the SQL;
fn arrow_type(&self, column_type: &str) -> Mapped.
Mapped { data_type: arrow_schema::DataType, fidelity: Fidelity }; Fidelity: Exact, Approximate(String), Lost(String).
Registry: with(Box<dyn Engine>) (a second engine of one id is ignored), get(id), ids().
Nothing crosses the trait as untyped JSON.
